# tree_matching:
# CSES 1130, Tree Matching (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1130), in our own words: a
# tree of n nodes, numbered 1 to n, given by its n - 1 edges; the most edges that can
# be chosen so that no two chosen edges share a node, a maximum matching. The input is
# the binary natural n (corpora/library/binary/natural), at least 1, and the edges, a
# Scott list (corpora/library/prelude/list) of pairs `pair a b`
# (corpora/library/prelude/pair) of binary naturals from 1 to n, which make a tree;
# the answer, the size of a maximum matching, is a binary natural. Part of the CSES
# port's fourth batch.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: every subset of the list of edges is built,
# those in which no two edges share a node are kept (the first edge of a subset shares
# a node with none of the later ones, and so on for each in turn), and the greatest
# size among them is taken. Its reading builds the 2^(n - 1) subsets of the edges; the
# replacement the family asks for is the greedy from the leaves, which in the reverse
# of a breadth-first order matches a node with its parent when neither is matched yet,
# in about n steps, on fixed-width integers. The number of nodes is not read, since
# the edges name every node that has one.
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ and application only:
# its text holds no top, no choice, no parallel and no literal. It β-reduces to V, the
# canonical binary numeral of the answer: every recursion ends, since subsets consumes
# the finite list of edges, and every other recursion consumes a finite list; the
# branches that a Scott boolean discards are never read. The program calls no
# subtraction. So ⊢_β P = V, and P ≃_O V by the soundness of the derivable equations
# for the contextual preorder of Definition 14 (Lean
# `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`): V is an answer, P
# ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then V ⊑_O W, while Böhm's
# theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and W to λx y. y, and applying
# both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and the second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "boolean")
λ true false _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons append map _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero _ _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ merge_binary_increment _ _ merge_binary_equality
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "order")
λ _ binary_maximum _
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self items
    . items (cons nil nil)
      λ head tail
      . ( λ rest
          . append (map (cons head) rest) rest
        ) λ. self tail
  )
λ subsets
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ first_edge second_edge
    . first_edge
      λ first_end second_end
      . second_edge
        λ third_end fourth_end
        . merge_binary_equality first_end third_end true
          ( merge_binary_equality first_end fourth_end true
            ( merge_binary_equality second_end third_end true
              (merge_binary_equality second_end fourth_end true false)
            )
          )
  )
λ shares
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self head items
    . items true λ other rest. shares head other false (self head rest)
  )
λ apart_from
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self items
    . items true λ head tail. apart_from head tail (self tail) false
  )
λ matching
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple λ. fixpoint λ self count items. items count λ _ tail. self (merge_binary_increment count) tail
  )
λ count_from
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self most subset_list
    . subset_list most
      λ subset rest
      . self (matching subset (binary_maximum most (count_from binary_zero subset)) most) rest
  )
λ largest
. (λtuple. tuple λ_ edges. largest binary_zero (subsets edges))
λ tree_matching
. export tree_matching
